  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2005-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The combined sum is \\(20 \\cdot 30 + 30 \\cdot 20 = 600 + 600\\) \\(= 1200.\\) The average of all \\(50\\) numbers is \\(\\dfrac{1200}{50} = 24.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "An average multiplied by the count gives the total sum",
        "Add the two totals, then divide by \\(50\\)"
